<div class=3D"ltx_para" id=3D"A5.SS1.p3">
<p class=3D"ltx_p" id=3D"A5.SS1.p3.1"><span class=3D"ltx_text ltx_font_bold=
" id=3D"A5.SS1.p3.1.1">Step 1.</span> GPT-5 (as the root LM) first decides =
to probe at the 1000 document list with regex queries. It has some priors a=
bout these events (as shown from its particular choice of words it looks fo=
r), but it also looks for specific keywords in the prompt like =E2=80=9Cbea=
uty pagent=E2=80=9D and =E2=80=9Cfestival=E2=80=9D.</p><button class=3D"sr-=
only button" style=3D"display: none;">Report issue for preceding element</b=
utton>
</div>
<div class=3D"ltx_para" id=3D"A5.SS1.p4">
<img alt=3D"[Uncaptioned image]" class=3D"ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" h=
eight=3D"294" id=3D"A5.SS1.p4.g1" src=3D"https://arxiv.org/html/2512.24601v=
2/trajectories/bcp-74_1.png" width=3D"476">
</div>
<div class=3D"ltx_para" id=3D"A5.SS1.p5">
<p class=3D"ltx_p" id=3D"A5.SS1.p5.1"><span class=3D"ltx_text ltx_font_bold=
" id=3D"A5.SS1.p5.1.1">Step 2.</span> After running its regex queries, the =
root LM finds an interesting snippet on the chunk at index 6, so it launche=
s a recursive LM call over this snippet to look for information relevant to=
 the original query. The RLM is able to both store this information in a va=
riable <span class=3D"ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" id=3D"A5.SS1.p5.1.2">an=
swer6</span>, as well as print this information out for the root LM to see.=
 The sub-LM call finds the answer is likely =E2=80=98Maria Dalmacio=E2=80=
=98 and stores this information back in the root LM=E2=80=99s environment.<=
/p><button class=3D"sr-only button" style=3D"display: none;">Report issue f=
or preceding element</button>
</div>
<div class=3D"ltx_para" id=3D"A5.SS1.p6">
<img alt=3D"[Uncaptioned image]" class=3D"ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" h=
eight=3D"183" id=3D"A5.SS1.p6.g1" src=3D"https://arxiv.org/html/2512.24601v=
2/trajectories/bcp-74_2-1.png" width=3D"476">
</div>
<div class=3D"ltx_para" id=3D"A5.SS1.p7">
<img alt=3D"[Uncaptioned image]" class=3D"ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" h=
