<p class=3D"ltx_p" id=3D"A5.SS4.p3.1"><span class=3D"ltx_text ltx_font_bold=
" id=3D"A5.SS4.p3.1.1">Step 1.</span> It is not always true that an input c=
ontext can be solved by partitioning it and recursively sub-querying models=
 over each partition, but in tasks that are not information dense, this is =
possible. In this case, the model chooses to break down the codebase into p=
arts and sub-query LMs to look for clues. The model then aggregates these c=
lues and provides a final answer as a separate sub-query.</p><button class=
=3D"sr-only button" style=3D"display: none;">Report issue for preceding ele=
ment</button>
</div>
